  "id": "humanoid",
  "description": "Shared animation set for the standard humanoid skeleton (backlog M1-21). Poses use joint terms, not raw bone axes: torso and head bend (+ forward), twist (+ to the character's left), lean (+ to its right); thighs swing (+ forward) and spread (+ outward); calves bend (+ knee flexes); feet point (+ toes down); upper arms swing (+ forward) and raise (+ sideways, away from the body); forearms bend (+ elbow flexes); hands curl (+ toward the palm) and cock (+ tips the end of the hand forward, which raises a blade held pointing forward). root: up/forward/left in metres, pitch (+ tips backward) in degrees. Unlisted joints return to rest. Keys may set ease ('in' accelerates into the key, e.g. a strike; 'out' snaps out of the previous key; 'linear'); the default is a smooth curve that never overshoots. overlap_s delays each joint family so extremities trail their parents (follow-through); auto_shrug raises the clavicles by that fraction of the arm's lift beyond 50 degrees forward or 25 degrees sideways, so shoulder armor rides up with the arm. tools/blender/animation.py converts all of this to bone rotations.",
